<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salta is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>, capital of Salta Province, in the Lerma valley. Founded in 1582 by Hernando de Lerma, it grew as a market for the mules sent to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potosi">Potosí</a>. During the wars of independence it was the base of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-miguel-de-guemes">Martín Miguel de Güemes</a>, whose gaucho forces held off royalist invasions from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-peru">Upper Peru</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salta.jpg" alt="Salta" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: loco085 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panor%C3%A1mica_Ciudad_de_Salta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Belgrano held Tucumán in 1812 and won at <b>Salta</b>, but lost at Vilcapugio and Ayohuma; Rondeau's Third campaign lost Upper Peru for good at Viluma on 29 November 1815.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-provinces-of-the-rio-de-la-plata">United Provinces of the Río de la Plata · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Governors founded a series of towns, including San Miguel de Tucumán in 1565, Córdoba in 1573, <b>Salta</b> in 1582 and San Salvador de Jujuy in 1593.</blockquote><a href="/state/governorate-of-tucuman">Governorate of Tucumán</a></li><li><blockquote>The republic faced constant conflict with <b>Salta</b>, governed by Martín Miguel de Güemes.</blockquote><a href="/state/republic-of-tucuman">Republic of Tucumán</a></li><li><blockquote>The league joined nine provinces, including Córdoba, Tucumán, <b>Salta</b>, Mendoza and San Juan, under Unitarian governors installed with Paz's backing.</blockquote><a href="/state/unitarian-league">Unitarian League</a></li></ul></section>
